    {
        "content": "<p>The pretty printer fails with error</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unknown</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">constant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`_private</span><span class=\"bp\">.«</span><span class=\"n\">external</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">///</span><span class=\"n\">MathlibDemo</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">MathlibDemo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"bp\">».</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">termℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I have seen this kind of thing before. The problem is related to the module system. (cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110024\">@Sebastian Ullrich</span>)</p>",
        "id": 577701601,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1772789648
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The pretty printer should either use the notation, or not. It shouldn't halfway try to use the notation and then fail with an error.</p>",
        "id": 577722768,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772795579
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem should be a missing <code>withoutExporting</code> somewhere. If <code>exporting</code> is set to true, then private declarations are invisible, which is exactly the error we are seeing.</p>",
